---
layout: layouts/base.njk
page_id: problems
page_width: medium
title: Sleep problems
eyebrow: Step 2
heading: What's keeping you up?
# The lede under the H1. `lede_tools` describes the filter and the area
# buttons, which need JavaScript, so it shows only once problems.js has shown
# them; `lede` is true either way. Together they are the meta description.
lede_tools: Open an area to see its topics, or search in your own words.
lede: Choose as many as sound like you.
eleventyComputed:
  summary: "{{ lede_tools }} {{ lede }}"
styles: ["pages/problems.css"]
scripts: ["problems.js"]
# The "When it happens" lanes, in display order. The ids are the
# time_of_day values in scripts/validate-content.js (TIMES_OF_DAY; a test
# keeps the two lists in step). Each lane's header colours are in
# src/css/pages/problems.css, keyed by id.
time_lanes:
  - { id: evening, label: "In the evening" }
  - { id: bedtime, label: "At bedtime" }
  - { id: night, label: "During the night" }
  - { id: early-morning, label: "Early morning" }
  - { id: day, label: "During the day" }
  - { id: any, label: "Any time" }
---
{#-
  Sleep problems (/problems/): SPEC §7.2, §8.1; HANDOFF §6.3; boards
  Problems-A.dc.html and Problems-Phone.dc.html.

  This page renders its own <main> and title band (on layouts/base.njk, not
  page.njk) because the filter, view toggle and result line sit inside the
  band. The band reuses the title-band classes from site.css.

  Without JavaScript (SPEC §2, §11):
    - every area is open, as a plain <h2> with its name, description and
      count; the problem links are always reachable;
    - the toolbar (filter, view toggle, Open/Close all), the lede's
      sentence about it and the "When it happens" lanes carry `hidden`, so
      no dead control is ever shown or described and no link is listed
      twice; the result line ("36 topics in 10 areas") stays, because it is
      true either way.
  src/js/problems.js turns each area heading's <span> into a
  <button aria-expanded aria-controls>, shows the toolbar, and runs the
  filter and the view switch. Hooks for it are data-* attributes; classes
  are for styling only.

  Analytics: this page sends no page_view (SPEC §10.2) and the filter sends
  nothing (§8.1), so there is no track_page_view here.

  Keywords: data/keywords.csv (SPEC §8.2, M2) becomes the global `keywords`.
  A problem's row, when there is one, is written to its list item's
  data-keywords for the filter; until the file exists nothing is written.
-#}
{%- from "partials/icons.njk" import icon -%}

{#- A problem's keywords from data/keywords.csv, or nothing. -#}
{%- macro keywordsFor(slug) -%}
{%- for row in keywords -%}{%- if row.page_id == slug -%}{{ row.keywords }}{%- endif -%}{%- endfor -%}
{%- endmacro -%}

{#- A link to a problem: short title (with the "New" pill), first-person
    line and, in the area rows, an arrow. Built on .topic-card
    (components.css); `variant` is "row" (By area) or "lane" (When it
    happens). The spaces between the spans keep the link's accessible name
    readable ("Tired but wired I'm tired, ..."). -#}
{%- macro topicCard(p, variant) -%}
<a class="topic-card topic-card--{{ variant }}" href="{{ p.url }}">
  <span class="topic-card__text">
    <span class="topic-card__title"><span data-topic-title>{{ p.title }}</span>{% if p.isNew %} <span class="topic-card__new">New</span>{% endif %}</span>
    <span class="topic-card__statement" data-topic-statement>{{ p.statement }}</span>
  </span>
  {%- if variant == 'row' %}
  {{ icon('arrow-right', 20, 'topic-card__arrow') }}
  {%- endif %}
</a>
{%- endmacro -%}

{%- set topicAreas = collections.problems | groupByArea(areas) -%}
{%- set total = collections.problems.length -%}
<main id="main" class="problems-page">
  <div class="band on-dark problems-band">
    <div class="band__inner container">
      <p class="band__eyebrow">{{ eyebrow }}</p>
      <h1 class="band__title">{{ heading }}</h1>
      <p class="band__lede"><span data-problems-hint hidden>{{ lede_tools }} </span>{{ lede }}</p>
      {#- Shown by problems.js once its handlers are attached. No <form> and
          no name: nothing is submitted, stored or sent (SPEC §8.1).
          autocomplete="off" keeps typed health terms out of the browser's
          form history and stops a stale value or view being restored. #}
      <div class="problems-tools" data-problems-tools hidden>
        <div class="problems-search">
          {#- Not "Search sleep problems": that is the header's site search,
              which leaves the page. This field only narrows the list here. #}
          <label class="problems-search__label" for="problem-filter">Find a sleep problem on this page</label>
          <input class="problems-search__input" id="problem-filter" type="search" placeholder="Try: night sweats, 3am, partner" autocomplete="off" spellcheck="false" aria-describedby="problem-filter-status" data-problem-filter>
        </div>
        <fieldset class="view-toggle">
          <legend class="visually-hidden">Group topics by</legend>
          <div class="view-toggle__options">
            <input class="view-toggle__input visually-hidden" type="radio" name="problems-view" id="view-area" value="area" checked autocomplete="off" data-view-choice>
            <label class="view-toggle__label" for="view-area">By area</label>
            <input class="view-toggle__input visually-hidden" type="radio" name="problems-view" id="view-time" value="time" autocomplete="off" data-view-choice>
            <label class="view-toggle__label" for="view-time">When it happens</label>
          </div>
        </fieldset>
        <button class="problems-tools__all" type="button" data-toggle-all>Open all areas</button>
      </div>
      <p class="problems-status" id="problem-filter-status" aria-live="polite" data-filter-status>{{ total }} topics in {{ topicAreas.length }} areas</p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="page-body container">
    <div class="problems" data-problems>
      {#- By area (the default view). Section ids are the area ids, so
          /problems/#core links to an area (SPEC §7.2). #}
      <div class="area-list" data-view-panel="area">
        {%- for area in topicAreas %}{% set n = area.problems.length %}
        <section class="area-list__area" id="{{ area.area_id }}">
          <h2 class="area-list__heading">
            <span class="area-list__header" data-area-header="{{ area.area_id }}">
              <span class="area-list__text">
                <span class="area-list__name" data-area-name>{{ area.name }}</span>
                <span class="area-list__description">{{ area.description }}</span>
              </span>
              <span class="area-list__count"><span data-area-count data-total="{{ n }}">{{ n }}</span><span class="area-list__count-unit"> {{ 'topic' if n == 1 else 'topics' }}</span></span>
              <span class="area-list__chevron" aria-hidden="true">{{ icon('chevron-down', 18) }}</span>
            </span>
          </h2>
          <ul class="area-list__problems" id="area-{{ area.area_id }}-problems" role="list" data-area-list>
            {%- for p in area.problems %}{% set kw = keywordsFor(p.slug) | trim %}
            <li data-slug="{{ p.slug }}"{% if kw | length %} data-keywords="{{ kw }}"{% endif %}>{{ topicCard(p, 'row') }}</li>
            {%- endfor %}
          </ul>
        </section>
        {%- endfor %}
      </div>

      {#- When it happens. Shown only by problems.js (the control that
          chooses it needs JavaScript); without it the areas above already
          list every problem once. Lane cards follow the collection order
          (area, then order within the area). #}
      <div class="time-lanes" data-view-panel="time" hidden>
        <ol class="time-lanes__list" role="list">
          {%- for lane in time_lanes %}
          {%- set laneProblems = [] %}
          {%- for item in collections.problems %}{% if item.data.time_of_day == lane.id and laneProblems.push(item) %}{% endif %}{% endfor %}
          {%- set n = laneProblems.length %}
          <li class="lane lane--{{ lane.id }}" data-lane>
            <h2 class="lane__header">{{ lane.label }} <span class="lane__count" data-lane-count>{{ n }} {{ 'topic' if n == 1 else 'topics' }}</span></h2>
            <ul class="lane__problems" role="list" data-lane-list{% if n == 0 %} hidden{% endif %}>
              {%- for item in laneProblems %}
              <li data-slug="{{ item.data.page_id }}">{{ topicCard({ title: item.data.title, statement: item.data.statement, url: item.url, isNew: item.data.new === true }, 'lane') }}</li>
              {%- endfor %}
            </ul>
          </li>
          {%- endfor %}
        </ol>
      </div>

      <div class="panel problems-nudge">
        <p class="problems-nudge__text">Haven't watched the introduction yet? It explains the ideas the other videos build on.</p>
        <p class="link-standalone"><a href="/start/">Go to the introduction</a></p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</main>
